                <pb facs="0571" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2788: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-19T15:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:23
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>107. Over 200 of the Carias leaders have been arrested in different parts of the
                    country since yesterday. One Congressman was killed and another [person?]
                    arrested by Government officers’ forces. The latter is a Justice of the Supreme
                    Court.</p>
                <p>It would appear that the Government’s defense has now turned out to be
                    persecution.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
